node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
*.log
release/

# A corpus must never live in the tree again. It is generated to
# ~/.cache/cc-miner by `pnpm -C cc-assay mine` and read from there at RUN time;
# nothing in this repo produces or consumes src/data any more.
#
# Kept as a rule anyway, because this exact accident has already happened: the
# directory's own .gitignore was deleted during a regeneration and 122 files of
# personal telemetry — conversation text, project names, cwd paths — were
# committed in its place. That guard lived inside the thing it guarded. This one
# does not.
pdum-cc-miner/src/data/

# Signing material, as a tripwire rather than a policy. Keys and certificates
# live OUTSIDE this tree by design (see DEPLOYMENT.md §2) — nothing here should
# ever match. But `git add -A` is how this repo gets committed, and a .p8 or a
# .p12 copied in "just for a second" is one command away from being public and
# unrevokable-in-history. Two of these also keep a key out of the app bundle:
# electron-builder's `files` allowlist includes electron/ and server/ wholesale.
*.p8
*.p12
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
AuthKey_*
*.keychain
*.keychain-db
